From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ashketchup <ashley@shuuri.net>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 11:05:49 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] mailbox: qcom-ipcc: remove IRQF_NO_SUSPEND across system
 suspend

Adopted from ROCKNIX (SM8550 0502, also Batocera 0013e16fa5).

The ADSP charger firmware pushes BATTMGR_NOTIFICATION over pmic_glink. Those
notifications ring the IPCC mailbox IRQ, which IRQF_NO_SUSPEND never masks
across system suspend, so it pulls the SoC out of deep sleep (the short
phantom wakes on USB). Co-processor doorbells no longer wake the AP while
asleep; pending signals are handled on resume.

Signed-off-by: Ashketchup <ashley@shuuri.net>
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-sonnet-5-5
Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/mailbox/qcom-ipcc.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/mailbox/qcom-ipcc.c b/drivers/mailbox/qcom-ipcc.c
index 185b63f724d4fba5a89ed55e7c3990857765c5a0..f2e5b9505bfcca1149db52092a98aa5f0281bbb1 100644
--- a/drivers/mailbox/qcom-ipcc.c
+++ b/drivers/mailbox/qcom-ipcc.c
@@ -326,7 +326,7 @@ static int qcom_ipcc_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 		goto err_mbox;
 
 	ret = devm_request_irq(&pdev->dev, ipcc->irq, qcom_ipcc_irq_fn,
-			       IRQF_TRIGGER_HIGH | IRQF_NO_SUSPEND |
+			       IRQF_TRIGGER_HIGH |
 			       IRQF_NO_THREAD, name, ipcc);
 	if (ret < 0)
 		goto err_req_irq;
